WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.790
The problem with the European Union today
is that they’re trying to dissolve the “nation-state”

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.900
and have a Europe of bureaucrats.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.680
That kind of approach is wrong for the United
States domestically.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.930
It’s wrong for the people of Europe.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.920
And there may be plenty of people around the
world that would like to see Europe come apart

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.420
because they misunderstand what the nature
of collective defense is.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:32.380
A “Europe of nations” as Charles de Gaulle
used to put it would suit the United States

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.380
just fine.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:39.230
I think that the current refugee and terrorism
crises in Europe demonstrate more convincingly

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:46.300
than any argument can that European institutions
are simply not sufficient to protect the people

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.490
of the continent.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:50.739
Security in Europe does not depend on the
European Union—

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:53.070
it depends on the NATO alliance.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.730
And NATO has one thing that the European Union
will never have

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.210
and that’s the United States.

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.239
That’s what people should focus on.

00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:06.500
When Britain leaves and becomes a stronger
partner in NATO again, everybody will be better

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:06.890
off.

